{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1252594-the-wolf-born-urazakh-angir","id":1252594,"title":"The Wolf Born: Urazakh-Angir","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-08T13:35:52-07:00","id":1252594,"title":"The Wolf Born: Urazakh-Angir","content":"I'm curious if anyone has ever used this character from Night Horrors: Wolfsbane. He just seems like the perfect antagonist to me, tying as he does into the origin myths of the Uratha, challenging the preconceptions of the Forsaken and serving as a Genghis Khan type warlord who could lead a seemingly unstoppable horde of Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T14:48:29-07:00","id":1252607,"title":"","content":"I haven't, but I've thought about it. In second edition I would be more likely to use something like the Pangaeans to challenge preconceived notions of the past, or Pangaean-era werewolves. As it is, while Urazakh was interesting, finding out about the specifics of it is something that would take a lot more investigation regarding the Pure than you would normally go to. If his pack came and started hassling you and calling him great, it wouldn't be that much different from a normal Pure pack doing it. Plus his mystery is built so that if you were able to dig into it, you might come across the flaws in the Pure idea of him as a messiah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T15:27:07-07:00","id":1252610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1252594-the-wolf-born-urazakh-angir?p=1252607#post1252607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't, but I've thought about it. In second edition I would be more likely to use something like the Pangaeans to challenge preconceived notions of the past, or Pangaean-era werewolves. As it is, while Urazakh was interesting, finding out about the specifics of it is something that would take a lot more investigation regarding the Pure than you would normally go to. If his pack came and started hassling you and calling him great, it wouldn't be that much different from a normal Pure pack doing it. Plus his mystery is built so that if you were able to dig into it, you might come across the flaws in the Pure idea of him as a messiah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, rather than his pack hassling you, I'd make Urazakh as a continent-wide threat to the Forsaken. Have him lead much; if not most; of the Pure, have his horde conquer territory after territory until it seems the Forsaken will be driven to the sea of whatever continent your set your story in and maybe discovering the holes into his claims of being the Messiah becomes the only way to stop him by ebbing away his support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}